findings.body:
Any authenticated caller can now pass `body.accountId` and receive the record for any account. The only guard is `auth(req)`, which authenticates the caller but does not authorize access to the target account.

```suggestion
  const caller = await auth(req);
  if (caller.role !== 'staff') {
    // only staff may look up other accounts
    throw new Response('forbidden', { status: 403 });
  }
  const id: string = body.accountId ?? caller.accountId;
```
